WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:00.697
(bell rings)

00:00:00.697 --> 00:00:01.174
- No.

00:00:01.174 --> 00:00:01.735
- Ow.
- [Ned] Ow.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.349
- Ah!

00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:05.437
- Young lady, if you don't
go to sleep in 30 seconds,

00:00:06.807 --> 00:00:09.528
it's gonna be bad news.

00:00:09.528 --> 00:00:12.811
Today, I'm going to learn
how to become a dad.

00:00:12.811 --> 00:00:15.209
(playful whimsical music)

00:00:15.209 --> 00:00:17.171
My wife and I are gonna have kids soon,

00:00:17.171 --> 00:00:19.991
but I'm completely
terrified and overwhelmed

00:00:19.991 --> 00:00:20.994
by that idea.

00:00:20.994 --> 00:00:23.458
It seems like it's a
huge change in your life.

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:24.690
Can you still have a date night?

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.863
Do you have to find a
babysitter every single time?

00:00:26.863 --> 00:00:28.336
- Being a dad is way harder than you think

00:00:28.336 --> 00:00:29.138
it's gonna be.

00:00:29.138 --> 00:00:30.601
Accepting that you're
not gonna be super dad

00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:32.365
or perfect is part of being a super dad--

00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:33.503
- Daddy, daddy.

00:00:33.503 --> 00:00:36.220
- I think often times you want things

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:37.681
to go one way and they
don't always go that way.

00:00:37.681 --> 00:00:38.626
- Shoes back on.
(bell dings)

00:00:38.626 --> 00:00:40.565
I'm gonna care for my friend Mike's kids

00:00:40.565 --> 00:00:43.762
for a whole day and I'll
see just how hard it is.

00:00:43.762 --> 00:00:44.947
- [Mike] Throw yourself into it--

00:00:44.947 --> 00:00:45.690
- [Ned] Ok.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:47.582
- And don't be afraid to do stuff.

00:00:47.582 --> 00:00:49.451
- You guys wanna take the
stairs or the elevator?

00:00:49.451 --> 00:00:50.611
- [Voiceover] Stairs.

00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:53.831
- Stairs, taking the stairs
was a difficult choice.

00:00:53.831 --> 00:00:56.214
Whew, I'm exhausted.

00:00:56.214 --> 00:00:58.153
- The other thing that's
really hard is patience.

00:00:58.153 --> 00:00:59.604
You've gotta have amazing patience

00:00:59.604 --> 00:01:00.847
when it comes to kids.

00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:01.891
- Do you guys like healthy snacks?

00:01:02.731 --> 00:01:03.683
- What about this?

00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:04.623
What about this?

00:01:04.623 --> 00:01:05.772
Can I have this?

00:01:05.772 --> 00:01:07.711
- Anne did you pick up something?

00:01:07.711 --> 00:01:08.605
- They're gonna annoy you.

00:01:08.605 --> 00:01:10.217
They're gonna take a
long time to do things,

00:01:10.217 --> 00:01:11.286
like brushing their teeth.

00:01:11.286 --> 00:01:12.717
They'll brush their teeth for 20 minutes.

00:01:12.717 --> 00:01:14.331
- No, no, no we don't eat ice cream.

00:01:14.331 --> 00:01:15.491
- [Girl] Ah!
- [Ned] Can't get

00:01:15.491 --> 00:01:18.858
a zebra print heart pillow,
you're not getting balls today.

00:01:18.858 --> 00:01:19.659
(girl screams)

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:20.541
- Gotta just wait.

00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:22.004
- Is he ok, or should we?

00:01:22.004 --> 00:01:23.281
- He's ok, I got the eyes in the back

00:01:23.281 --> 00:01:24.302
of the head watching.

00:01:24.302 --> 00:01:25.197
- What is that?

00:01:25.197 --> 00:01:26.844
Why are you hitting my head?

00:01:26.844 --> 00:01:28.145
- Kids love to play pretend,

00:01:28.145 --> 00:01:29.037
but one of the things that you're gonna--

00:01:29.037 --> 00:01:29.647
(child groans)

00:01:29.647 --> 00:01:30.610
- We'll take that back.

00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:31.446
- One of the tough--

00:01:31.446 --> 00:01:32.948
(child screams)
(Ned laughs)

00:01:32.948 --> 00:01:34.563
James, shh.

00:01:34.563 --> 00:01:35.746
- One more time.

00:01:35.746 --> 00:01:37.186
- One of the tough things
about playing pretend

00:01:37.186 --> 00:01:39.751
with your kids is that
it takes a lot of mental,

00:01:39.751 --> 00:01:41.552
like concentration.

00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:43.956
- This whole castle's made of cookies.

00:01:43.956 --> 00:01:46.671
- That's right, this whole
castle's made of cookies

00:01:46.671 --> 00:01:48.309
and a cookie moster.

00:01:48.309 --> 00:01:49.331
(Ned snarls)

00:01:49.331 --> 00:01:50.155
(girl laughs)

00:01:50.155 --> 00:01:52.454
Well this is fun you guys,
we're just hanging out.

00:01:52.454 --> 00:01:55.591
Oh boy, James, James, James, ok.

00:01:55.591 --> 00:01:57.519
- It's time to go to the ball.

00:01:57.519 --> 00:01:59.492
- We're all going to the ball.

00:01:59.492 --> 00:02:00.933
You don't ok there James?

00:02:00.933 --> 00:02:02.720
(playful music)

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.675
Pose the dolls next to each other.

00:02:04.675 --> 00:02:07.885
- We love Daddy, we love Daddy.

00:02:08.935 --> 00:02:10.874
- Daddy's not here anymore.

00:02:10.874 --> 00:02:12.417
- One of the tough things
about being a parent,

00:02:12.417 --> 00:02:14.297
especially with this age, is making sure

00:02:14.297 --> 00:02:15.692
that they eat healthy food.

00:02:15.692 --> 00:02:19.654
- If you eat the broccoli,
then I will give you the candy.

00:02:19.654 --> 00:02:20.920
Do we have a deal?

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:21.874
Oh no!

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:24.162
- It's good to not make a
big show of it being weird.

00:02:24.162 --> 00:02:25.463
(Ned chugs toy)

00:02:25.463 --> 00:02:26.769
- Woo woo!

00:02:27.622 --> 00:02:30.260
Broccoli delivery for Captain James.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.490
- And you've gotta eat it yourself

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:32.628
'cause if they see that you eat,

00:02:32.628 --> 00:02:33.627
then they'll wanna eat it.

00:02:33.627 --> 00:02:35.101
(Ned snarls)

00:02:35.101 --> 00:02:37.956
(laughter erupts)

00:02:37.956 --> 00:02:39.137
- Got it.

00:02:39.137 --> 00:02:43.188
Once you tip your hand that
there's C-A-N-D-Y somewhere--

00:02:43.188 --> 00:02:43.843
- [Mike] You should probably,

00:02:43.843 --> 00:02:44.899
you and I should probably stop

00:02:44.899 --> 00:02:46.512
even spelling out the word candy.

00:02:46.512 --> 00:02:47.361
- [Ned] Oh really?

00:02:47.361 --> 00:02:48.800
- You should have like
a safe word, you know,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.100
call it like asparagus.

00:02:50.100 --> 00:02:53.040
- Would you rather have the
lollipop or the broccoli.

00:02:53.040 --> 00:02:55.060
(sweet orchestral music)

00:02:55.060 --> 00:02:57.231
(laughter erupts)

00:02:57.231 --> 00:02:58.383
Classic.

00:02:58.383 --> 00:02:59.997
- Putting your kids to bed
is definitely difficult,

00:02:59.997 --> 00:03:02.239
because kids don't wanna go to bed.

00:03:02.239 --> 00:03:03.782
- Bouncy, bouncy, bounce.

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:04.861
- Can't bounce too much.

00:03:04.861 --> 00:03:05.882
How many stories do you normally

00:03:05.882 --> 00:03:06.974
have before bed?

00:03:06.974 --> 00:03:08.542
- 600 million.

00:03:08.542 --> 00:03:10.202
- 600 million?

00:03:10.202 --> 00:03:10.840
Why?

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.560
I love sleep.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:12.477
(yawns)

00:03:12.477 --> 00:03:13.997
I really am getting sleepy.

00:03:13.997 --> 00:03:15.076
- So they're gonna fight you on it

00:03:15.076 --> 00:03:17.341
and they've tried to stretch
out that time routine

00:03:17.341 --> 00:03:18.978
as long as it can possibly be.

00:03:18.978 --> 00:03:19.860
- Ready for bed.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:20.975
- Another one.

00:03:20.975 --> 00:03:25.734
- Ok, bass drums are big,
but whistles are little.

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.973
(blows music)

00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:29.345
Wait now I said we're
only doing two books.

00:03:29.345 --> 00:03:30.192
- Last book.

00:03:30.192 --> 00:03:31.131
- We're only doing two books.

00:03:31.131 --> 00:03:32.134
- Last book.

00:03:32.134 --> 00:03:36.188
- We're reading, apparently,
as many books as it takes.

00:03:36.188 --> 00:03:37.639
(girl claps)

00:03:37.639 --> 00:03:40.599
I stirred it all together, it was yummy,

00:03:40.599 --> 00:03:42.477
but it wasn't pink.

00:03:44.408 --> 00:03:48.095
And that is the end of Pinklicious.

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:53.899
(sweet violin music)

00:03:55.461 --> 00:03:58.368
- And that's how you stay awake.

00:03:58.368 --> 00:04:00.783
- I was only with the kids
for a small period of time.

00:04:00.783 --> 00:04:03.847
I want to go into a hot bubble bath

00:04:03.847 --> 00:04:05.624
and drink white wine.

00:04:05.624 --> 00:04:06.668
How did I do?

00:04:06.668 --> 00:04:08.944
- You know, I think you
did actually really well.

00:04:08.944 --> 00:04:11.104
You were really engaged,
you were really dedicated,

00:04:11.104 --> 00:04:12.405
and you were trying really hard.

00:04:12.405 --> 00:04:14.099
- Even though it was really difficult

00:04:14.099 --> 00:04:16.386
and exhausting on my body,

00:04:16.386 --> 00:04:19.926
seeing the way Mike
interacted with his kids

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:23.512
and how much they loved
him and he loved them,

00:04:23.512 --> 00:04:25.734
that was, it was such a nice feeling.

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.907
Thumbs up or thumbs down,
how do you think I did?

00:04:27.907 --> 00:04:28.556
Now.

00:04:28.556 --> 00:04:29.288
- Sideways.

00:04:29.288 --> 00:04:30.576
- So I've got some work to do.

00:04:30.576 --> 00:04:32.654
I think of all the things
that my dad did for me

00:04:32.654 --> 00:04:34.053
and I'm so thankful.

00:04:34.053 --> 00:04:35.597
- So what do you think,
do you think your ready

00:04:35.597 --> 00:04:38.175
to possibly in the near
future take the leap?

00:04:38.175 --> 00:04:39.259
- I'm gonna call my wife.

00:04:39.259 --> 00:04:40.122
How's it going?

00:04:40.122 --> 00:04:42.879
I've been shooting the video
on taking care of a toddler.

00:04:44.346 --> 00:04:45.897
I hope so, yea.

00:04:46.983 --> 00:04:48.590
It seems really hard.

00:04:48.590 --> 00:04:51.411
(laughs nervously)

00:04:51.411 --> 00:04:53.848
Wee, let's make babies.

00:04:53.848 --> 00:04:56.512
(laughs nervously)

00:04:56.512 --> 00:04:57.474
- [Voiceover] Bye, I love you.

00:04:57.474 --> 00:04:59.425
- [Ned] Bye, I love you too.

00:04:59.425 --> 00:05:01.852
She said, "let's make babies."

00:05:01.852 --> 00:05:06.530
Which is pretty awesome
as well as terrifying.

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.566
(orchestral music)

